<div class="guide-styles" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Best in Slot Gear list for Feral Druid Tank in Cataclysm Classic pre-raid. Gear in this guide is obtained from a multitude of sources, but mostly from <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a> and <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=3148/fissure-stone-fragment">
<span>
<img alt="Fissure Stone Fragment" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_talisman_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fissure Stone Fragment</span></span></a>, and some Binds on Equipped items.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">
<span class="c11">Best in Slot Gear for Feral Druid Tank in Pre-Raid</span></h2>Feral Druid Tank stat priority is not straightforward as it heavily depends on your uptime of <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=768/cat-form">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_druid_catform.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Cat Form</span></a>, if you're the Main-Tank you want to mostly focus on survivability, while if you're the Off-Tank you will likely spend a lot of time in <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=768/cat-form">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_druid_catform.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Cat Form</span></a> so you want to focus more on stats that increase both survivability and damage done. Main stat is always king for Feral Druids, Stamina, and Agility are by far your best stats, and therefore the main focus will always be to wear the highest item level item available to you.<br/>
<br/>This general guideline for stat priority for Feral Druid Tanks will be split into Main-Tank and Off-Tank, where Off-Tank is the role where you spend a lot of time in <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=768/cat-form">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_druid_catform.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Cat Form</span></a> and Main-Tank is the role where you spend all your time <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=5487/bear-form">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_racial_bearform.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bear Form</span></a>, most Feral Druid Tank players will likely be somewhere in between these two. The Off-Tank role is more relevant in farm raids, as for progression this next rule is the most important. <b>If you're ever tanking anything for the first time, both as Off-Tank and Main-Tank, always prioritize going as defensive as possible</b>, and then build your way to a more offensive build over time as your raid and especially Healers get more gear and more confidence on the fights.<ul>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<b>Main-Tank</b> - When you're main-tanking you should aim to be as tanky as possible, you want to prioritize Stamina (<a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=52242/solid-ocean-sapphire">
<img alt="Solid Ocean Sapphire" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cutgemsuperior2.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Solid Ocean Sapphire</span></a>) in sockets and for most of your enchants. For reforging and your preferred secondary stats, you want to prioritize Dodge as it gives you the most survivability, Mastery is the second-best defensive stat and Critical Strike is the third-best defensive stat. Dodge is quite ahead of Mastery and Critical Strike, while the latter two are fairly even and directly scale off of each other as Mastery increases your self-absorb through <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=77494/savage-defender">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_racial_cannibalize.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Savage Defender</span></a>'s effect on <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=62600/savage-defense">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_racial_cannibalize.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Savage Defense</span></a>, and <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=62600/savage-defense">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_racial_cannibalize.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Savage Defense</span></a> only gives that absorb when you critically strike.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<b>Off-Tank</b> - When you're off-tanking you will likely find yourself in <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=768/cat-form">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_druid_catform.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Cat Form</span></a> quite a bit, you still want to prioritize Stamina (<a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=52242/solid-ocean-sapphire">
<img alt="Solid Ocean Sapphire" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cutgemsuperior2.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Solid Ocean Sapphire</span></a>) in most of your sockets, but for your enchants you want to use more of the Agility options. For reforging and your preferred secondary stats, Mastery will be your most wanted secondary stat as it increases your damage the most in <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=768/cat-form">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_druid_catform.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Cat Form</span></a> and still gives you survivability in <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=5487/bear-form">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_racial_bearform.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bear Form</span></a>. Expertise and Critical Strike become your second-most favored secondary stats, where Critical Strike is more defensive while Expertise is more offensive. When your raid and the Healers have gotten some gear and confidence on fights you can start thinking about swapping out some of the <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=52242/solid-ocean-sapphire">
<img alt="Solid Ocean Sapphire" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cutgemsuperior2.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Solid Ocean Sapphire</span></a> with <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=52212/delicate-inferno-ruby">
<img alt="Delicate Inferno Ruby" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cutgemsuperior6.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Delicate Inferno Ruby</span></a>.</div></li></ul>
<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="valor-points">
<span class="c11">Valor Points for Feral Druid Tank Phase 3</span></h3>
<i>
<a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a> will be converted to <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=395/justice-points">
<span>
<img alt="Justice Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-justice.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Justice Points</span></span></a> once a new phase drops, and with that new <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a> items will be added. There's a weekly cap of 1600 from doing raids and Heroic dungeons, and each week adds another 1600 to the cap, allowing you to farm <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a> for weeks you might've missed.</i>
<br/>Your main priority will be to get your 2-set bonus as early as possible, and then use the rest to acquire upgrades in the slots where the highest item level upgrade is. Which gear you should go for first depends on what gear you have, which is why the list isn't meant to be followed blindly, but rather as a guideline. If an item will increase your Agility more than an item that's higher on the list, you should probably go for the item that increases your Agility more unless there's a set bonus. To make sure you're always getting the most damage per <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a>, use <a href="https://wowsims.github.io/cata/druid/feral" target="_blank">WoWSims</a> to simulate what will give you more output. <br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=71146/covenant-of-the-flame">
<img alt="Covenant of the Flame" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_scroll_15.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Covenant of the Flame</span></a> is high on the list even though it likely isn't the biggest upgrade because it is the only item that can not be replaced in the raid and can be upgraded into <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=71567/covenant-of-the-flame">
<img alt="Covenant of the Flame" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_scroll_15.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Covenant of the Flame</span></a>, which is your Best in Slot Relic, with a <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=71617/crystallized-firestone">
<img alt="Crystallized Firestone" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_diablostone.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Crystallized Firestone</span></a>.<br/>
<br/>
